    "created_at": "2021-07-13T16:52:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-07-13T16:52:24Z",
    "body": "My take is that this is a good incremental improvement that prevents us from using the longhand syntax on future APIs.\r\n\r\nLonger-term, I think it'd be best to move stringifiers to just be operations the same we did for serializer -> toJSON(). That is, remove the stringifier concept, and just let people add their own `toString()` operations. We could add something like `[ForwardsTo=href]` if we want to allow omitting the method steps, but I'm not sure whether that's necessary.\r\n\r\nThat longer-term change requires a bit of spec ecosystem churn so I'm not sure how worthwhile it is.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
